# Project Bootstrap

## Project

- Name: declaracoes-gov-core
- Type: Java Library (JAR)
- Language: Java 8+
- Build: Maven 3.9+

## Key Constraints

1. Java 8 compatibility - no `var`, no Java 9+ Optional methods
2. Thread-safe public APIs required
3. No Spring/Jakarta EE dependencies
4. Framework-agnostic core
5. Immutable value objects preferred
6. BigDecimal for monetary values

## Architecture

```
certificado/  - Certificate management (A1/A3, mTLS)
assinatura/   - XML digital signature (RSA-SHA256, C14N)
documento/    - Validators (CNPJ alphanumeric, CPF, IE)
json/         - JSON utilities (Jackson wrapper)
exception/    - Common exceptions
```

## Quality Gates

- `mvn verify` must pass
- 80% line coverage minimum
- Checkstyle clean
- PMD clean

## Code Patterns

### Value Object
```java
public final class CNPJ {
    private final String value;
    
    private CNPJ(String value) {
        this.value = validate(value);
    }
    
    public static CNPJ of(String value) {
        return new CNPJ(value);
    }
    
    // getters, equals, hashCode, toString
}
```

### Thread-Safe Service
```java
/**
 * @apiNote This class is thread-safe.
 */
public final class XmlSigner {
    // stateless or immutable fields
}
```

## Security

- Never commit certificates (.p12, .pfx, .pem)
- Never log passwords or private keys
- Clear sensitive arrays immediately after use
- Use test keystores with dummy credentials only
